  "Number": 17,
  "Question": "Let \\(w,\\) \\(x,\\) \\(y,\\) and \\(z\\) be whole numbers. If \\[2^w \\cdot 3^x \\cdot 5^y \\cdot 7^z = 588,\\] then what does \\[2w + 3x + 5y + 7z\\] equal?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(21\\)",
    "B": "\\(25\\)",
    "C": "\\(27\\)",
    "D": "\\(35\\)",
    "E": "\\(56\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The bases \\(2,3,5,7\\) are prime, so the exponents count how many copies of each prime occur in the factorization of \\(588\\). Factor it as\n\\[\n588=4\\cdot147=2^2\\cdot3\\cdot7^2.\n\\]\nMatching the prime factors gives \\(w=2\\), \\(x=1\\), and \\(z=2\\). There is no factor of \\(5\\), so \\(y=0\\); this is allowed because whole numbers include zero and \\(5^0=1\\).\n\nSubstituting into the requested expression,\n\\[\n2w+3x+5y+7z\n=2(2)+3(1)+5(0)+7(2)\n=21.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice A.",
